[case_guidance] case_id | kind | ordinal | item
"C-3d6d2adfd3" | "avoid" | 0 | "Moving the same decision tree into trivial helpers solely to hide its score."
"C-3d6d2adfd3" | "lead" | 0 | "Clarify early exits and simplify nested decisions."
"C-3d6d2adfd3" | "lead" | 1 | "Examine whether variants deserve meaningful abstractions."
"C-4063b2b57c" | "avoid" | 0 | "Renaming or aliasing a collaborator solely to split the access count."
"C-4063b2b57c" | "lead" | 0 | "Review each qualifying foreign value and its contributing accesses."
"C-4063b2b57c" | "lead" | 1 | "Consider moving cohesive behavior toward the owner of that data."
"C-4fb5041cb7" | "avoid" | 0 | "Introducing a facade or moving code solely to lower the dependency count."
"C-4fb5041cb7" | "avoid" | 1 | "Treating a lower dependency score as proof of a better design."
"C-4fb5041cb7" | "lead" | 0 | "Does the caller know details its dependency could own?"
"C-4fb5041cb7" | "lead" | 1 | "Is policy repeated across boundaries?"
"C-4fb5041cb7" | "lead" | 2 | "Are behavioral assumptions explicit in the contract?"
"C-4fb5041cb7" | "lead" | 3 | "Do these dependencies support one cohesive operation?"
"C-4fb5041cb7" | "lead" | 4 | "Compare supplied arguments and consumed results with types appearing only in signatures or discarded results; origin lists overlap and do not alter the score."
"C-5522b4859c" | "avoid" | 0 | "Creating stepOne/stepTwo/stepThree helpers solely to satisfy metrics."
"C-5522b4859c" | "avoid" | 1 | "Treating a meaningful name as proof of a meaningful boundary."
"C-5522b4859c" | "avoid" | 2 | "Suppressing the case without documented justification."
"C-5522b4859c" | "lead" | 0 | "Review the qualifying helpers with their shared inputs and dependencies."
"C-5522b4859c" | "lead" | 1 | "Establish cohesive boundaries with distinct ownership and collaboration."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "avoid" | 0 | "Adding wrapper objects, broad visitor protocols, or no-op methods solely to clear the finding without improving cohesion or reducing coupling."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "avoid" | 1 | "Moving each decision into a differently named helper while retaining the repeated variant knowledge."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "avoid" | 2 | "Replacing switches with equivalent if/else chains."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "avoid" | 3 | "Introducing an interface while callers still select concrete implementations repeatedly."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "avoid" | 4 | "Renaming constants, aliases, variables, or files solely to evade correlation."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "lead" | 0 | "Examine whether callers can send the same message to interchangeable role players instead of selecting behavior themselves."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "lead" | 1 | "If the variants select implementations, use a factory or construction boundary to select once and return a common behavioral role; callers then send messages through that role."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "lead" | 2 | "If independent operations inspect the same variants, evaluate a visitor or adapter with one dispatch boundary; keep operation-specific behavior, traversal policy, and results with each operation."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "lead" | 3 | "If branches merely map variants to data, consider a data-driven representation owned near the variant definition."
"C-82bc134f4f" | "lead" | 4 | "Move behavior toward the object or role that has the knowledge required to perform it."
"C-ad03ea5957" | "avoid" | 0 | "Bundling unrelated inputs into an opaque bag solely to reduce the count."
"C-ad03ea5957" | "lead" | 0 | "Examine whether inputs form a cohesive domain object."
"C-ad03ea5957" | "lead" | 1 | "Separate responsibilities that require different inputs."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "avoid" | 0 | "Moving only the switch into a helper that still exposes concrete implementation details to the caller."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "avoid" | 1 | "Wrapping the concrete implementations in another facade solely to reduce the finding."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "avoid" | 2 | "Renaming constructors, variables, or implementations."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "avoid" | 3 | "Extracting branch bodies while leaving selection and collaboration in the same function."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "lead" | 0 | "Consider moving implementation selection into a factory or composition boundary that returns the role."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "lead" | 1 | "Consider accepting the role as a dependency instead of deciding which concrete player to use here."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "lead" | 2 | "Keep collaboration expressed in terms of the role while centralizing knowledge of concrete implementations."
"C-b06ec7d1d9" | "lead" | 3 | "The selected implementations already respond to the same required messages. Consider expressing that collaboration as a role owned by the consumer."
"C-b10bccb46b" | "avoid" | 0 | "Extracting arbitrary helpers solely to reduce the line count."
"C-b10bccb46b" | "avoid" | 1 | "Moving the same procedure into another file."
"C-b10bccb46b" | "lead" | 0 | "Look for cohesive responsibilities with different reasons to change."
"C-b10bccb46b" | "lead" | 1 | "Move behavior toward the object that owns its data."
"C-b79a56258e" | "avoid" | 0 | "Bundling unrelated values solely to silence the repeated-parameter rule."
"C-b79a56258e" | "lead" | 0 | "Inspect the participating signatures for a shared domain concept."
"C-b79a56258e" | "lead" | 1 | "Introduce a parameter object only if the values belong together."
"C-b79a56258e" | "lead" | 2 | "Every member of this clump has a primitive type. Consider a distinct named type for each kind of value, such as one ID type per identifier; the type checker would then see the clump and reject values passed in each other's place."
"C-bd6e66f9ad" | "avoid" | 0 | "Deleting a comment that describes an untested invariant without first preserving that invariant in a regression test."
"C-bd6e66f9ad" | "avoid" | 1 | "Disguising prose as a machine directive, generated code, or an unused string."
"C-bd6e66f9ad" | "avoid" | 2 | "Writing tests that merely assert comment absence instead of the behavior the comment was intended to protect."
"C-bd6e66f9ad" | "lead" | 0 | "If a comment preserves an intentional omission or guards against a future fix, write a regression test that fails when the unwanted behavior is introduced. Comments are not a reliable enforcement mechanism."
"C-bd6e66f9ad" | "lead" | 1 | "Express intent through clear names, cohesive structure, and executable contracts; preserve useful design rationale in external documentation."
"C-bd6e66f9ad" | "lead" | 2 | "Remove obsolete explanations and commented-out code after preserving any required behavior in tests."
"C-cf8ec1ee12" | "avoid" | 0 | "Bundling unrelated inputs into an opaque bag solely to reduce the count."
"C-cf8ec1ee12" | "lead" | 0 | "Examine whether inputs form a cohesive domain object."
"C-cf8ec1ee12" | "lead" | 1 | "Separate responsibilities that require different inputs."

